Bug: /luxon/src/datetime.js `get isInDST()` (around line 1164) currently reads:
```js
  get isInDST() {
    if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
      return false;
    } else {
      return (
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1 }).offset || this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
      );
    }
  }
```
This mis-detects DST in years where the standard offset is not the minimum offset of the year, e.g. the USA in 1974 (year-round DST: DST began Jan 6, 1974 and ended Oct 27, 1974). `DateTime.local(1974, 1, 6).isInDST()` wrongly returns false.

Apply exactly this change: replace `this.set({ month: 1 })` with `this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 })`, i.e. the body becomes:
```js
  get isInDST() {
    if (this.isOffsetFixed) {
      return false;
    } else {
      return (
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 1, day: 1 }).offset ||
        this.offset > this.set({ month: 5 }).offset
      );
    }
  }
```
Do not change anything else in src/datetime.js.

Then VERIFY:
- Create a temp jest project OUTSIDE test/: /luxon/tmp-dst-verify/jest.config.js with rootDir "/luxon", roots ["tmp-dst-verify"], testEnvironment "node", and a transform using babel-jest with the repo's .babelrc (copy the pattern from /luxon/jest.config.js). Add /luxon/tmp-dst-verify/t.test.js that, with `process.env.TZ = 'America/New_York'` set before importing (or by using `{ zone: 'America/New_York' }`), asserts: `DateTime.fromObject({year:1974,month:1,day:6},{zone:'America/New_York'}).isInDST === true`; same for 1974-10-27; `DateTime.fromObject({year:1974,month:12,day:1},{zone:'America/New_York'}).isInDST === false`; `DateTime.fromObject({year:2019,month:1,day:1},{zone:'America/New_York'}).isInDST === false`; `DateTime.fromObject({year:2019,month:7,day:1},{zone:'America/New_York'}).isInDST === true`; and that a UTC DateTime `isInDST === false`. Run `cd /luxon && npx jest --config tmp-dst-verify/jest.config.js` and report output. Then `rm -rf /luxon/tmp-dst-verify`.
- Run `cd /luxon && npx jest test/datetime 2>&1 | tail -20` and `cd /luxon && npx jest 2>&1 | tail -20`; report summaries. The only pre-existing failures allowed are the 2 French-ICU ones in test/datetime/toFormat.test.js.

Do NOT modify anything under /luxon/test/. Report the final isInDST code and the test output.
